From 011a82af8b2421085ef434636b56c96c169295c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:47:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] wifi: brcmfmac: of: read the country code map on every
 bus

brcmf_of_probe() reads brcm,ccode-map and brcm,ccode-map-trivial only
from nodes compatible with "brcm,bcm4329-fmac". The binding also allows
the PCIe compatibles ("pci14e4,4425" and so on) that Apple ARM64 device
trees use, but those nodes never have that compatible, so the driver
ignores the map there.

Without a map, brcmf_cfg80211_reg_notifier() can't translate the
country cfg80211 settles on (from the user or the AP's country element)
and returns, so the firmware keeps the worldwide default from the NVRAM
(ccode=XZ on Apple boards) whatever the regulatory domain is.

Read the map from any device tree node. Keep reading the MAC address and
the SDIO settings only from "brcm,bcm4329-fmac" nodes, as before.

Signed-off-by: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/of.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/of.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/of.c
index 03efae36a0b2..1d8a85c6d244 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/of.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/of.c
@@ -121,13 +121,19 @@ int brcmf_of_probe(struct device *dev, enum brcmf_bus_type bus_type,
 
 	brcmf_dbg(INFO, "%s LPO clock\n", clk ? "enable" : "no");
 
-	if (!np || !of_device_is_compatible(np, "brcm,bcm4329-fmac"))
+	if (!np)
 		return 0;
 
+	/* The country code map applies to every bus, not only SDIO: Apple
+	 * ARM64 platforms describe their PCIe chips with "pci14e4,..." only.
+	 */
 	err = brcmf_of_get_country_codes(dev, settings);
 	if (err)
 		brcmf_err("failed to get OF country code map (err=%d)\n", err);
 
+	if (!of_device_is_compatible(np, "brcm,bcm4329-fmac"))
+		return 0;
+
 	err = of_get_mac_address(np, settings->mac);
 	if (err == -EPROBE_DEFER)
 		return err;
